### Description

Custom LSP servers are matched by fileTypes, but textDocument/didOpen always sets languageId from the built-in detectLanguageId()
 map. Unknown extensions (e.g. .gd) fall back to "plaintext".

 There is no lsp.json field to override languageId. Servers that require a real id (Godot expects "gdscript") ignore the document,
 so definition/hover/diagnostics return empty even when the server is connected.

 Routing works; document open does not.

 Relevant code:
 - packages/coding-agent/src/lsp/client.ts — ensureFileOpen uses detectLanguageId(filePath)
 - packages/coding-agent/src/utils/lang-from-path.ts — unknown ext → "plaintext"
 - packages/coding-agent/src/lsp/config.ts — fileTypes used only for server selection

### Steps to Reproduce

1. Add a minimal fake LSP and project config:

 .omp/lsp.json

 ```json
   {
     "servers": {
       "fake-gd": {
         "command": "node",
         "args": [".omp/fake-lsp.mjs"],
         "fileTypes": [".gd"],
         "rootMarkers": [".omp"]
       }
     }
   }
 ```

 .omp/fake-lsp.mjs

 ```js
   #!/usr/bin/env node
   import fs from "node:fs";

   const logPath = new URL("./fake-lsp.log", import.meta.url);
   const log = (line) => fs.appendFileSync(logPath, line + "\n");

   let buf = Buffer.alloc(0);
   process.stdin.on("data", (chunk) => {
     buf = Buffer.concat([buf, chunk]);
     while (true) {
       const sep = buf.indexOf("\r\n\r\n");
       if (sep < 0) break;
       const header = buf.slice(0, sep).toString("utf8");
       const m = header.match(/Content-Length:\s*(\d+)/i);
       if (!m) { buf = buf.slice(sep + 4); continue; }
       const len = Number(m[1]);
       const start = sep + 4;
       if (buf.length < start + len) break;
       const body = buf.slice(start, start + len).toString("utf8");
       buf = buf.slice(start + len);
       let msg; try { msg = JSON.parse(body); } catch { continue; }

       if (msg.method === "initialize") {
         respond(msg.id, {
           capabilities: {
             textDocumentSync: { openClose: true, change: 1 },
             definitionProvider: true,
           },
         });
       } else if (msg.method === "textDocument/didOpen") {
         const td = msg.params?.textDocument;
         log(JSON.stringify({ uri: td?.uri, languageId: td?.languageId }));
       } else if (msg.method === "textDocument/definition" && msg.id != null) {
         respond(msg.id, []);
       } else if (msg.method === "shutdown") {
         respond(msg.id, null);
       }
     }
   });

   function respond(id, result) {
     const payload = JSON.stringify({ jsonrpc: "2.0", id, result });
     process.stdout.write(
       `Content-Length: ${Buffer.byteLength(payload)}\r\n\r\n${payload}`,
     );
   }
 ```

 2. Create any foo.gd (contents irrelevant).
 3. Restart OMP (LSP config is process-cached).
 4. Run the LSP tool: definition/hover/diagnostics on foo.gd (anything that opens the document).
 5. Inspect .omp/fake-lsp.log.

### Expected Behavior

 - didOpen uses a configurable or sensible languageId for the custom server (e.g. config "languageId": "gdscript", or at least not
 an unconditional "plaintext" for server-handled extensions).
 - Ideal config shape:
   ```json
     {
       "servers": {
         "gdscript": {
           "command": "godot-lsp-stdio-bridge",
           "fileTypes": [".gd", ".gdshader"],
           "languageId": "gdscript",
           "rootMarkers": ["project.godot"]
         }
       }
     }
   ```

 Actual: log shows "languageId":"plaintext". With Godot + godot-lsp-stdio-bridge, the same plaintext didOpen yields empty
 definition/hover; rewriting to "gdscript" fixes it.



### Error Output

```shell

```

### Platform

Windows (native)

### omp version

17.1.5

### Bun version

unknown

### Provider

None

### Area

None

### Additional context

 Related: opencode#23663 (https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/issues/23663), opencode#20526
 (https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/issues/20526), opencode#32023 (https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/issues/32023)

